**What the oracle actually does (now pinned in the spec)**
- **c1**: anon nodes get `'#' + <object id>` from the shared object-id counter (nodes/edges/groups all draw from it); the **parser resets the counter at each parse** (deterministic names — `#1`, `#3` for `[ a ] --> [ ] --> [ ]`), while API `add_anon_node` continues it across the process; anon nodes carry a default `label: ' '`
- **c2**: every assigned value passes the store-layer unquote (`set_attribute('label','"hello world"')` stores `hello world`); `border` is **decomposed at assignment** into border-style/width/color (never stored verbatim) and **recomposed on read** — `'dotted bold red'` reads back `'bold  red'`; class-scope attrs stored separately, instance reads override
- **c3**: edges store **group objects** as endpoints (`Graph::Easy::Group -> Graph::Easy::Group`), never rewritten to members; bare `( A ) --> ( B )` yields 2 groups + 1 edge and zero nodes; `as_txt` renders the groups but drops the group-to-group edge
- **c3/p3 (delete lifecycle)**: `del_node` drops the node **and all incident edges**; a later `add_edge('A','B')` **succeeds**, re-creating A as a fresh bare node (color reads back as class default `black`; old edges not revived)

